DSHMap.receive("pkg","@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-voice-input-bundle",{"readme":"# @deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-voice-input-bundle\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis optional bundle composes a speech Service Definition, local SenseVoice provider, authenticated Remote and browser microphone control. Shipped profiles leave it disabled.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Use this package](#use-this-package)\n- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)\n- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)\n- [Model Experience](#model-experience)\n- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)\n- [Dev Note](#dev-note)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"use-this-package\"></a>\n## Use this package\n\nOpen Plugins in the Web sidebar and enable Voice Input, marked by a blue waveform icon. If models need preparation, a dialog offers Go to setup or Later; Go to setup opens the bundle details. Complete caches need no setup prompt. In the details, choose Download and prepare; the collapsed current-step summary expands to the complete step list. Downloads report actual bytes; verification and loading show elapsed time. Once ready, click the microphone between the model selector and Send, then Stop to insert a transcript. Bundle details store the recognizer and language through the Settings service. Disabling the bundle cancels active work; cached assets remain on disk.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"understand-the-implementation\"></a>\n## Understand the implementation\n\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer details — click to expand</summary>\n\nThe static `cordis.patch.yml` adds the four voice rows, selects `sensevoice-local` as the default recognizer and supplies the provider cache directory with `dshHomePath`. Optional-bundle installation makes the package available to management without selecting it in default profiles. The browser contribution owns its generated Remote mount; stable API Remotes do not import experimental code.\n\n</details>\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"further-exploration\"></a>\n## Further Exploration\n\n[Voice input subsystem](../../../docs/subsystems/voice-input.md)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"model-experience\"></a>\n## Model Experience\n\nNone, as recordings and preparation remain outside model requests; ordinary user submission owns any later text.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nNo direct effect; ordinary submission owns the message content.\n\n## Known Limitations and Deferred Work\n\n<a id=\"known-limitations-and-deferred-work\"></a>\n\n- The initial bundle supplies one local recognizer. Additional providers register with the same service under distinct ids; cloud recognition requires an explicit new provider and credential configuration. The bundle does not add a model tool or change the agent loop.\n- Installing dsh also installs `sherpa-onnx-node` and its platform-specific native runtime, including ONNX Runtime, even when this bundle is disabled. Runtime installation adds disk and download costs separate from the models downloaded by Download and prepare; the native package size varies by platform and version.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"dev-note\"></a>\n### Dev Note\n\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer details — click to expand</summary>\n\nNone.\n\n</details>\n","modelExperience":"None, as recordings and preparation remain outside model requests; ordinary user submission owns any later text.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nNo direct effect; ordinary submission owns the message content.","limitations":"- The initial bundle supplies one local recognizer. Additional providers register with the same service under distinct ids; cloud recognition requires an explicit new provider and credential configuration. The bundle does not add a model tool or change the agent loop.\n- Installing dsh also installs `sherpa-onnx-node` and its platform-specific native runtime, including ONNX Runtime, even when this bundle is disabled. Runtime installation adds disk and download costs separate from the models downloaded by Download and prepare; the native package size varies by platform and version.\n\n-----","files":[["README.i18n.yaml",37,1583,"o"],["README.md",77,3187,"o"],["README.zh.md",77,2875,"o"],["cordis.patch.yml",13,520,"o"],["icon.svg",9,701,"o"],["locale/en.json",6,159,"o"],["locale/zh.json",6,143,"o"],["package.json",54,1543,"o"],["src/index.ts",2,94,"s"],["tsconfig.json",15,227,"o"],["tsdown.config.ts",3,219,"o"]],"sources":{"README.md":"---\ndescription: \"Enable experimental speech input from the plugin manager.\"\nkind: \"package-bundle\"\n---\n\n# @deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-voice-input-bundle\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis optional bundle composes a speech Service Definition, local SenseVoice provider, authenticated Remote and browser microphone control. Shipped profiles leave it disabled.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Use this package](#use-this-package)\n- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)\n- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)\n- [Model Experience](#model-experience)\n- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)\n- [Dev Note](#dev-note)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"use-this-package\"></a>\n## Use this package\n\nOpen Plugins in the Web sidebar and enable Voice Input, marked by a blue waveform icon. If models need preparation, a dialog offers Go to setup or Later; Go to setup opens the bundle details. Complete caches need no setup prompt. In the details, choose Download and prepare; the collapsed current-step summary expands to the complete step list. Downloads report actual bytes; verification and loading show elapsed time. Once ready, click the microphone between the model selector and Send, then Stop to insert a transcript. Bundle details store the recognizer and language through the Settings service. Disabling the bundle cancels active work; cached assets remain on disk.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"understand-the-implementation\"></a>\n## Understand the implementation\n\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer details — click to expand</summary>\n\nThe static `cordis.patch.yml` adds the four voice rows, selects `sensevoice-local` as the default recognizer and supplies the provider cache directory with `dshHomePath`. Optional-bundle installation makes the package available to management without selecting it in default profiles. The browser contribution owns its generated Remote mount; stable API Remotes do not import experimental code.\n\n</details>\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"further-exploration\"></a>\n## Further Exploration\n\n[Voice input subsystem](../../../docs/subsystems/voice-input.md)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"model-experience\"></a>\n## Model Experience\n\nNone, as recordings and preparation remain outside model requests; ordinary user submission owns any later text.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nNo direct effect; ordinary submission owns the message content.\n\n## Known Limitations and Deferred Work\n\n<a id=\"known-limitations-and-deferred-work\"></a>\n\n- The initial bundle supplies one local recognizer. Additional providers register with the same service under distinct ids; cloud recognition requires an explicit new provider and credential configuration. The bundle does not add a model tool or change the agent loop.\n- Installing dsh also installs `sherpa-onnx-node` and its platform-specific native runtime, including ONNX Runtime, even when this bundle is disabled. Runtime installation adds disk and download costs separate from the models downloaded by Download and prepare; the native package size varies by platform and version.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"dev-note\"></a>\n### Dev Note\n\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer details — click to expand</summary>\n\nNone.\n\n</details>\n","cordis.patch.yml":"- insert:\n    - id: speech-to-text\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-speech-to-text'\n      config:\n        defaultProvider: sensevoice-local\n    - id: speech-to-text-sensevoice\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-speech-to-text-sensevoice'\n      config:\n        dataRoot: !!js dshHomePath('speech-to-text', 'sensevoice')\n    - id: api-speech-to-text\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-api-speech-to-text'\n    - id: ui-voice-input\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-client-ui-voice-input'\n","icon.svg":"<svg width=\"36\" height=\"36\" viewBox=\"0 0 36 36\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <path d=\"M23.7324 8.77148V27.2295L21.2324 27.2285V8.77051L23.7324 8.77148ZM14.6797 10.7715L14.6787 25.2295L12.1787 25.2285L12.1797 10.7705L14.6797 10.7715ZM19.3926 22.4131H16.8926V13.5859H19.3926V22.4131ZM10.0625 20.708H7.5625V15.291H10.0625V20.708ZM28.4375 20.708H25.9375V15.291H28.4375V20.708Z\" fill=\"url(#paint0_linear_3371_85203)\" />\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"paint0_linear_3371_85203\" x1=\"8.24602\" y1=\"16.4083\" x2=\"32.5611\" y2=\"22.9699\" gradientUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\">\n      <stop stop-color=\"#67C7FE\" />\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#3F77D8\" />\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n</svg>\n","locale/en.json":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"title\": \"Voice input\",\n    \"description\": \"Transcribe recordings locally with SenseVoice; first use requires installing dependencies\"\n  }\n}\n","locale/zh.json":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"title\": \"语音输入\",\n    \"description\": \"在本机使用 SenseVoice 转写录音，首次使用需安装依赖。\"\n  }\n}\n","package.json":"{\n  \"name\": \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-voice-input-bundle\",\n  \"description\": \"Experimental voice input with local SenseVoice; downloads its runtime on first use\",\n  \"version\": \"0.2.1-rc.2\",\n  \"icon\": \"./icon.svg\",\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"access\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness.git\",\n    \"directory\": \"packages/experimental/voice-input-bundle\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"main\": \"lib/index.js\",\n  \"types\": \"lib/types/index.d.ts\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./lib/types/index.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./lib/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./src/*\": \"./src/*\",\n    \"./package.json\": \"./package.json\",\n    \"./cordis.patch.yml\": \"./cordis.patch.yml\",\n    \"./locale/*.json\": \"./locale/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"icon.svg\",\n    \"locale/*.json\",\n    \"lib/index.js\",\n    \"cordis.patch.yml\",\n    \"lib/types/**/*.d.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-speech-to-text\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-speech-to-text-sensevoice\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-api-speech-to-text\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-client-ui-voice-input\": \"workspace:*\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": \"workspace:~\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": \"workspace:~\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-include\": \"workspace:~\",\n    \"js-yaml\": \"^4.3.2\"\n  },\n  \"dsh\": {\n    \"bundle\": {\n      \"patch\": \"./cordis.patch.yml\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n","src/index.ts":"/** Experimental voice input composition; runtime rows live in cordis.patch.yml. */\nexport {}\n","tsconfig.json":"{\n  \"extends\": \"../../../tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"rootDir\": \"src\",\n    \"outDir\": \"lib/types\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src\"\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"../../../vendor/cordis\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","tsdown.config.ts":"import { defineConfig } from 'tsdown'\n\nexport default defineConfig({ entry: ['lib/types/index.js'], outDir: 'lib', format: ['esm'], platform: 'node', target: 'es2024', fixedExtension: false, dts: false, clean: false })\n"},"symbols":{"defs":[],"files":{},"api":[],"uses":{}}});
